<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-acetabularia-acetabulum-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Acetabularia acetabulum Turing wavelength at 25.28 µm (Holocene, detail scale) (Acetabularia acetabulum)",
        "Acetabularia acetabulum Turing wavelength at 25.28 µm (Holocene, detail scale) faithfully reproduces Acetabularia acetabulum morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-acetabularia-acetabulum-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-acetabularia-acetabulum-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-acetabularia-acetabulum-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-acetabularia-acetabulum-turing-wavelength-s0-4> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-acetabularia-acetabulum-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Acetabularia acetabulum specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-acetabularia-acetabulum-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Acetabularia acetabulum" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A measured value for the axial/hoop diffusivity ratio.",
        "does_not_claim: A second chronospecies, or any reuse of sibling slot 192's template constants.",
        "does_not_claim: Pixel identity with the CC0 photograph or the gallery plate.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Axial/hoop sweep showing the ridge axis flips as the ratio crosses 1.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Diffusivities placing the fastest mode at 25.43 µm, next to the 25.28 µm tier length.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Seeded grain on the face-on cap, not a copy of the photograph.",
        "reported_in_source: Dumais & Harrison 2000: reaction-diffusion is the favoured whorl mechanism in Acetabularia.",
        "reported_in_source: Holloway & Harrison 2007: Brusselator kinetics on a plant surface can make whorls.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952: diffusion-driven instability and the critical wavenumber.",
        "transfer_boundary: 25.28 µm is the slot's tier length. The papers discuss whorl spacing without publishing this number.",
        "transfer_boundary: The model disk (radius 354 µm) is the geometry implied by 88 ridges at that wavelength, not a traced outline of the adult CC0 cap." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Acetabularia acetabulum" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "IV. Protista & Monera" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Mineralized Protists (Silica/Calcite)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Acetabularia" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-acetabularia-acetabulum-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/acetabularia_acetabulum_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif; organism: Acetabularia acetabulum; environment: python 3.12.3, note Pass 2 on the same VM. Nanopub profile absent, so the KG is unsigned.; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952: diffusion-driven instability and the critical wavenumber. | Dumais & Harrison 2000: reaction-diffusion is the favoured whorl mechanism in Acetabularia. | Holloway & Harrison 2007: Brusselator kinetics on a plant surface can make whorls.; reconstructed_in_script: Diffusivities placing the fastest mode at 25.43 µm, next to the 25.28 µm tier length. | Axial/hoop sweep showing the ridge axis flips as the ratio crosses 1. | Seeded grain on the face-on cap, not a copy of the photograph.; transfer_boundary: 25.28 µm is the slot's tier length. The papers discuss whorl spacing without publishing this number. | The model disk (radius 354 µm) is the geometry implied by 88 ridges at that wavelength, not a traced outline of the adult CC0 cap.; does_not_claim: Pixel identity with the CC0 photograph or the gallery plate. | A measured value for the axial/hoop diffusivity ratio. | A second chronospecies, or any reuse of sibling slot 192's template constants.]; phenomenon_size: 41 µm (4.096e-05 m, log10=-4.388 m, tier=4_cellular_10um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 41 µm to 6.7 cm): 41 µm:acetabularia-acetabulum-bioelectric-polarity, 79 µm:acetabularia-acetabulum-vertex-packing, 1.5 mm:acetabularia-acetabulum-turing-wavelength, 2.8 mm:acetabularia-acetabulum-clock-wavefront, 6.3 mm:acetabularia-acetabulum-elastic-buckling, 8.7 mm:acetabularia-acetabulum-morphogen-condensation, 1.1 cm:acetabularia-acetabulum-flux-canalization, 1.5 cm:acetabularia-acetabulum-branching-tree" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/s0022-5193(88)80213-3>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1093/aob/mcm295>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.2000.0565> ;
    pk:geologicalAgeMa 0e+00 ;
    pk:geologicalPeriod "Holocene (Extant)" ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-acetabularia-acetabulum-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-acetabularia-acetabulum-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity>,
